.TH CJSON_DICTIONARY_SET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cjson_dictionary_set \- set or replace a key in an object node
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cjson.h>

ccol_retval_t cjson_dictionary_set(cjson obj, const char *key, cjson child);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Inserts or replaces the value for key in obj.  Ownership of child
transfers to obj unconditionally: on success the object owns child;
on failure child is deep-freed by cjson_dictionary_set.  Do not free
child after calling this function regardless of the return value.
If a previous child existed under key it is deep-freed before the
new one is stored.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success, ccol_invalid_args, or ccol_not_enough_memory.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cjson_dictionary_get (3),
.BR cjson_create_dictionary (3)
